ent communications supported by voice and messaging solutions; integrated payment solutions embedded in intake and post-visit workflows, and financing solutions that enable healthcare organizations to accelerate cash collections while offering flexible payment options to patients; and digital intake and clinical data capture, patient engagement and activation tools, and measurement and analytics solutions. It also offers PhreesiaPads, a self-service intake tablets; and Arrivals Kiosks, which are on-site kiosks. The company serves a range of healthcare organizations including ambulatory practices, health systems, and hospitals, as well as life sciences companies, government entities, patient advocacy, public interest and not-for-profit and other organizations. Phreesia, Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is based in Wilmington, Delaware.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chaim  Indig | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $515,000 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $269K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 25%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $38K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $38K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Phreesia, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $788M market cap on $481M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -96% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $68M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 34.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin -1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 6.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.08962940227335855},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): durably derated by the market; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Phreesia Inc. (PHR) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/Precision_Trading_with_Phreesia_Inc._PHR_Risk_Zones_111326012002_1794550802.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794550802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Phreesia (NYSE:PHR) Shares Gap Down After Analyst Downgrade","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/phreesia-nysephr-shares-gap-down-after-analyst-downgrade.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794410491.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.412,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"(PHR) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/15/PHR_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_110326013602_1793687762.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793687762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AQR Capital Management Reports 4.3% Ownership Stake in Phreesia, Inc.","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/aqr-capital-management-reports-43-ownership-stake-in-phreesia-inc","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577134.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Phreesia Sets Release Date for Fiscal Third Quarter 2027 Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"htt